@*
    OdsPopupMenu: ONE real <button> trigger with a MudMenu popover anchored over it (issue #255).
    It is the shared host behind every select-style Ods control (OdsMultiSelect, OdsSortSelect,
    OdsTypeSelect, OdsPageSizeSelect, OdsInlineSelect, OdsTagMultiSelect, OdsMoneyField's currency
    picker, AccountSmartTagAdder, CreateTransactionDialog's account picker).

    Why it exists: MudMenu wraps a custom ActivatorContent in its own
    <div tabindex="0" role="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="…">. Every Ods trigger put a
    real <button> inside that div, which gave each control two tab stops (an unnamed "button", then
    the real one), announced a button nested in a button, and left aria-expanded on the div rather
    than on the focused, named control. So nothing here uses ActivatorContent.

    Instead the MudMenu is rendered with NO activator at all (no ActivatorContent, Label or Icon),
    which MudMenu supports: it then draws only its popover and its click-away overlay. The menu's
    root element is stretched over this component's box (.odc-popmenu-anchor, position:absolute;
    inset:0; pointer-events:none), because MudBlazor positions a popover against the parent of its
    placeholder, i.e. that root — so the popover still anchors, flips and sizes against the trigger
    exactly as before, and still portals out of any overflow:hidden ancestor.

    What this component owns, once, for every consumer:
      • the trigger's aria-haspopup / aria-expanded, on the button itself;
      • open / close: a click (pointer or the button's own Enter/Space) toggles; MudMenu's overlay
        closes on an outside click;
      • focus return: a close that did not start on the trigger sends focus back to it, so focus is
        never stranded on <body> when the popover's content unmounts;
      • the single-choice keyboard contract, when RowId/RowCount are set: ↑/↓ on the closed
        trigger opens; opening focuses the selected row (else the first); ↑/↓/Home/End rove and
        clamp; Esc closes and restores focus; Tab closes behind itself. Rows are the consumer's own
        <button role="menuitemradio" tabindex="-1"> elements, which call RowKeyDownAsync.

    A MudMenuItem needs MudMenu's own activator to receive keyboard focus (MudMenu tracks the
    focused item from keydowns on its root, which this trigger is deliberately not inside), so a
    consumer renders its rows as buttons rather than MudMenuItems — the pattern OdsTypeSelect set.
    OdsMenu, whose rows ARE MudMenuItems, uses MudMenu's built-in icon-button activator instead.
*@

@inject IJSRuntime Js

<div class="@WrapperClass" @attributes="UserAttributes">
    @BeforeTrigger
    <button @ref="_trigger"
            type="button"
            id="@EffectiveTriggerId"
            class="@TriggerClassName"
            disabled="@Disabled"
            aria-haspopup="@HasPopup"
            aria-expanded="@(_open ? "true" : "false")"
            aria-label="@AriaLabel"
            aria-describedby="@AriaDescribedBy"
            aria-invalid="@(AriaInvalid ? "true" : null)"
            @onclick="OnTriggerClickAsync"
            @onkeydown="OnTriggerKeyDownAsync">
        @TriggerContent
    </button>
    <MudMenu @ref="_menu"
             Class="odc-popmenu-anchor"
             AnchorOrigin="@AnchorOrigin"
             TransformOrigin="@TransformOrigin"
             PopoverClass="@PopoverClass"
             ListClass="@ListClass"
             RelativeWidth="@RelativeWidth"
             MaxHeight="@MaxHeight"
             Disabled="@Disabled"
             OpenChanged="OnMenuOpenChangedAsync">
        @ChildContent
    </MudMenu>
</div>
